properties.description:
A core test file, nine tests, pinning the class rather than one writer:
- every declared twin is an edge that can join its node type;
- a finding written through the generic writer, and a by-hand report, hang from their subject;
- a moved subject takes its edge with it;
- a writer that draws its own copy gets exactly one;
- an import out of step repairs the missing copy, the second subject (moved to ABOUT_ENTITY) and the retired flow values, names each repair, and reports nothing when run again;
- a snapshot outlives its node without a repair;
- the refusal names the property and ABOUT_ENTITY;
- an out-of-step RocksDB store is repaired on reopen and keeps the report.
A companion MCP test, crates/reflow2-mcp/tests/a_stored_twin_is_kept_by_the_store.rs, pins the tool doors: the generic create_node, create_edge, create_edges (all or nothing) and delete_edge.
